        given-names: "T. S."
    title: "Revisiting Spacetrack Report #3"
    collection-title: "AIAA/AAS Astrodynamics Specialist Conference"
    number: "AIAA 2006-6753"
    year: 2006
    notes: >-
      The published verification set SGP4-VER.TLE and tcppver.out, read at run
      time out of the installed sgp4 distribution as package data and reproduced
      to 1.154503e-07 km in validation/validate_sgp4_vectors.py.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Vallado
        given-names: "D. A."
    title: "Fundamentals of Astrodynamics and Applications"
    edition: "4th"
    publisher:
      name: "Microcosm Press"
    year: 2013
    notes: >-
      Algorithm 9 and Algorithm 10 for the element conversions, Algorithm 2 for
      Kepler's equation, Algorithm 29 for the Sun and Algorithm 31 for the Moon,
      eq. (3-47) for Greenwich mean sidereal time, eq. (8-58) for the J2
      acceleration the generic Legendre code is checked against, section 3.2.2
      for Bowring's geodetic height, Table 8-4 for the piecewise exponential
      atmosphere, and section 9.4 for the B* relation.
  - type: article
    authors:
      - family-names: Bowring
        given-names: "B. R."
    title: "The accuracy of geodetic latitude and height equations"
    journal: "Survey Review"
    volume: 28
    issue: 218
    year: 1985
    notes: >-
      The closed-form geodetic height in orbitdrift.frames. Its departure from a
      converged fixed-point solution grows with altitude and is measured rather
      than quoted: 1.219 mm at 400 km, 15.488 mm at 1700 km.
  - type: book
    authors:
      - family-names: Montenbruck
        given-names: "O."
      - family-names: Gill
        given-names: "E."
    title: "Satellite Orbits: Models, Methods and Applications"
